WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:06.381
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:19.060
During the age of the dinosaurs, spectacular species

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.440
like this Pachycephalosaur attract the most attention.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.609
But the prehistoric world was also home

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.905
to a wide variety of other quite different species.

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:33.783
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:42.292
So what were some of the animals living alongside the dinosaurs?

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:45.211
[GROWLING]

00:00:47.672 --> 00:00:54.012
One of the most surprising was this--

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:56.848
[GROWLING]

00:00:58.766 --> 00:01:03.188
The biggest frog to have ever lived.

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:06.649
Beelzebufo was an especially large wide-bodied frog

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:08.651
with a proportionally large head.

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:16.743
It was the size of a small dog, a fearsome hunter

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:20.622
with an appearance to match.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:23.791
It had armored skull bones and armored backbone

00:01:23.791 --> 00:01:29.005
heavily reinforced and big strong jaws.

00:01:29.005 --> 00:01:33.009
Beelzebufo had an especially powerful bite.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:35.887
It would have been able to grab and subdue and kill

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:39.724
even relatively large prey up to the size of baby dinosaurs.

00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:47.023
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:47.023 --> 00:01:52.278
The oceans were dominated not by dinosaurs

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.072
but by marine reptiles.

00:01:58.826 --> 00:02:01.371
The largest were mosasaurs.

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:09.879
These giant marine lizards could reach 50 feet in length

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:11.631
and weigh 15 tons.

00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:19.138
They had massively elongate powerful jaws, huge jaw

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:22.684
muscles, and enormous conical teeth.

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:26.646
[SPLASHING]

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:32.360
They were the greatest marine predators of all time.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.196
[SPLASHING]

00:02:38.032 --> 00:02:45.331
But while giant lizards like this mosasaur ruled the oceans,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.668
a very different group of reptiles filled the skies.

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:52.296
[SQUAWKING]

00:02:52.296 --> 00:02:54.799
In the air, we've got this fantastic diversity

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:58.678
of flying reptiles that we call pterosaurs.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.930
These things are often referred to as flying dinosaurs,

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:01.764
but they're not.

00:03:04.642 --> 00:03:07.687
These were the very first animals with backbones to fly.

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:18.865
Their wingspan ranged from 10 inches to an enormous 33 feet.

00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:24.037
The largest posed a deadly threat

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.081
for even the most fearsome of dinosaurs.

00:03:27.081 --> 00:03:30.042
[GROWLING]

00:03:34.964 --> 00:03:36.924
They were not just very big.

00:03:36.924 --> 00:03:40.011
They also had a skull that was about 3 meters long

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:42.472
and ended in giant stabby jaws.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:48.644
If you were tyrannosaurus, you would probably

00:03:48.644 --> 00:03:51.981
think twice about approaching an animal that dangerous.

00:03:55.443 --> 00:03:58.404
[TRUMPETING]

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:10.124
Many of the impressive creatures on the prehistoric planet

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:13.336
looked completely different from anything alive today.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:21.594
But there were also some animals that might

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.471
seem a little more familiar--

00:04:27.475 --> 00:04:27.975
Mammals.

00:04:33.314 --> 00:04:35.775
Despite people thinking that the Cretaceous was

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:39.111
all about dinosaurs, there were tons of mammals.

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:42.782
We find things that lived in the water like beavers today.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.117
We see things that were running around in the trees

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.703
and even gliding and things that were living under the ground

00:04:47.703 --> 00:04:49.372
and digging into the soil.

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:52.542
And you see mammals evolved a lot of characteristics

00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:55.002
related to being able to move around at night.

00:04:58.339 --> 00:05:01.884
These lifestyles may have been important in helping

00:05:01.884 --> 00:05:05.346
mammals avoid the dinosaurs living alongside them.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.020
They evolved a lot of different tools

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.065
to help them survive during that period--

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:22.113
fur, being warm blooded, even evolving big brains

00:05:22.113 --> 00:05:26.701
and sensory structures that allow them to see at nighttime.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:29.704
In fact, we may have dinosaurs to thank for the way mammals

00:05:29.704 --> 00:05:30.204
look today.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:39.714
After 150 million years, the dinosaurs

00:05:39.714 --> 00:05:42.883
were wiped out by a massive meteor strike.

00:05:45.761 --> 00:05:49.640
In their place, mammals became the dominant life

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:54.437
on planet Earth as they still are today.

